<main>

    <div id="single-main">
        <img width="640" height="427" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-3374172_s.jpg" class="ofi wp-post-image" alt="Getting to Sendai" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-3374172_s.jpg 640w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-3374172_s-380x254.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" />        
        <div id="block-head-pos">
        	<h1><span>Getting to Sendai</span></h1>
        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="editor-wrapper" id="menu-colorchange-flg">
        <div class="editor-styles-wrapper cf">
			
                        
                        
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/2-Sendai_Airport_01.jpg" alt="Sendai_Airport" class="wp-image-553" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/2-Sendai_Airport_01.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/2-Sendai_Airport_01-768x432.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/2-Sendai_Airport_01-380x214.jpg 380w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Flying in to Sendai Airport from Abroad</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Flights to Sendai Airport from overseas are listed below.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Direct flights operate from Seoul, two cities in Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Bangkok to Sendai Airport.<br>Charter flights are occasionally operated from Malaysia. Flights from China (Beijing, Dalian, and Shanghai) are currently suspended.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Domestically, Sendai Airport is connected to eight cities within Japan. Passengers arriving at Nagoya or Kansai International Airports can transfer to a domestic flight to reach Sendai Airport.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-table is-thead"><table class="has-fixed-layout"><tbody><tr><td>Route</td><td>Weeklly Flight number</td><td>Flight Time</td><td>Airlines</td></tr><tr><td>Seoul</td><td>5 flights /week</td><td>2 hr 5 mins</td><td>Asiana Airlines</td></tr><tr><td>Beijing (via Dalian)</td><td>*Currently suspended</td><td> 5 hr 10 mins </td><td>Air China</td></tr><tr><td>Shanghai</td><td>*Currently suspended</td><td> 2 hr 45 mins </td><td> Air China </td></tr><tr><td>Taipei</td><td> 17 flights /week </td><td> 3 hr 25 mins </td><td>Eva Air, Tigerair Taiwan and STARLUX Airlines</td></tr><tr><td>Kaohsiung</td><td><meta charset="utf-8"> 3 flights /week </td><td><meta charset="utf-8"> 4 hr 10 mins</td><td><meta charset="utf-8">Tigerair Taiwan</td></tr><tr><td>Hong Kong</td><td><meta charset="utf-8"> 6 flights /week </td><td>5 hrs</td><td>GREATER BAY AIRLINES and HK Express<br>*GREATER BAY AIRLINES<br>Scheduled to resume in Winter.</td></tr><tr><td>Bangkok<br>Don Mueang Airport (DMK)</td><td><meta charset="utf-8"></meta> 4 flights /week<br>*Flights operate seasonally.<br>Schedule subject to change.</td><td><meta charset="utf-8"> 7 hr 30 mins</td><td><strong>Thai AirAsia X</strong><br></td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">International Flights (as of Jun 5, 2026)</figcaption></figure>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://www.sendai-airport.co.jp/en/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Sendai International Airport </a></div>
</div>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-css-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading h-ttl1">Access from Tokyo to Sendai</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/3-shinkansen1.jpg" alt="shinkansen" class="wp-image-554" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/3-shinkansen1.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/3-shinkansen1-768x432.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/3-shinkansen1-380x214.jpg 380w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="500" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/4-jrpass.png" alt="jrpass" class="wp-image-555" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/4-jrpass.png 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/4-jrpass-768x375.png 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/4-jrpass-380x186.png 380w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Shinkansen (Bullet Train)</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you want to save time, taking Shinkansen (bullet train) is the best way.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"> It takes only about one and a half hour from Tokyo to Sendai and the price is about 10,890yen for one-way. More than 80 trains run between Tokyo and Sendai daily.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br>For foreign visitors, “Japan Rail Pass”, “JR East Pass Tohoku Area” and “JR East and South Hokkaido Rail Pass” are recommendable so that you can take the train cheaper than normal price.<br></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can reserve seat via JR East website (below).</p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://www.jreast.co.jp/multi/en/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><span style="font-size: 2.2rem;">JR EAST</span> </a></div>
</div>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="681" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/5-Sendai_station.jpg" alt="Sendai_station" class="wp-image-556" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/5-Sendai_station.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/5-Sendai_station-768x511.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/5-Sendai_station-380x253.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Long-distance Bus</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you take a long-distance bus from Tokyo to Sendai, you can save money. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Many bus companies have a line between Tokyo and Sendai. It takes about five and a half hours and the fare is 2,200yen ~ 6,500yen (depends on bus company, time schedule and bus grade). There are direct lines from Narita airport and Haneda airport to Sendai as well.</p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://willerexpress.com/en/?mid=960" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><span style="font-size: 2.2rem;">Willer Express</span> </a></div>



<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://japanbusonline.com/en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><span style="font-size: 2.2rem;">Japan Bus Online</span> </a></div>
</div>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-css-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading h-ttl1">Ferries and Other Access to Sendai</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/6-ferry1.jpg" alt="ferry" class="wp-image-557" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/6-ferry1.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/6-ferry1-768x432.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/6-ferry1-380x214.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/7-ferry2.jpg" alt="ferry" class="wp-image-558" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/7-ferry2.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/7-ferry2-768x432.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/7-ferry2-380x214.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Access to Sendai from Other Cities in Japan</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sendai is connected to other cities by the Shinkansen or other train lines, buses, and ferries. The list below shows access to Sendai from other cities (prices listed are adult one-way fares.)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">●Tomakomai-Sendai: Ferry &#8211; 14 hrs 45 min ¥8300<br>・From Tomakomai to Sendai: leave at 19:00, arrive at 10:00 (next day)<br>・From Sendai to Tomakomai: leave at 19:40, arrive at 11:00 (next day)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">●Nagoya-Sendai: Ferry &#8211; 21 hrs ¥7200<br>・From Nagoya to Sendai: leave at 19:00, arrive at 16:40 (next day)<br>・From Sendai to Nagoya: leave at 12:50, arrive at 10:30 (next day)</p>



